{:edb/db-before-t 2295 :edb/db-after-t 2296 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535608 50 #inst "2026-10-09T03:26:40.417Z" 13194139535608 true] [17592186157290 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357359 13194139535608 true] [17592186157290 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357366 13194139535608 true] [17592186157292 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357338 13194139535608 true] [17592186157305 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357345 13194139535608 true] [17592186157305 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357352 13194139535608 true] [17592186357338 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357339 13194139535608 true] [17592186357338 1089 "q-106623" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357338 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535608 true] [17592186357338 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.$" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357338 1113 #uuid "aa5fba2b-b9cd-5f9f-94be-1d958a9dbda2" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357338 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent Identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{5}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{5} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}+1 & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357339 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357340 13194139535608 true] [17592186357339 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357341 13194139535608 true] [17592186357339 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357342 13194139535608 true] [17592186357339 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357343 13194139535608 true] [17592186357339 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357344 13194139535608 true] [17592186357339 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535608 true] [17592186357339 1041 "selection" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357339 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357343 13194139535608 true] [17592186357339 1110 #uuid "39104662-f3eb-59ae-b338-4ddf553f285d" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357340 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357340 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535608 true] [17592186357340 1111 #uuid "dccf38bb-e173-596a-a5e6-40e2594426b4" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357341 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357341 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535608 true] [17592186357341 1111 #uuid "9c2b9737-4208-54a4-9641-00ec2aed40cb" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357342 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}=1" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357342 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535608 true] [17592186357342 1111 #uuid "a80e0f67-361c-5a78-886b-0c8034ed8c0a" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357343 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}=1" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357343 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535608 true] [17592186357343 1111 #uuid "a62cfca6-edc1-51c2-865e-f477b4e6129c" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357344 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}=1" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357344 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535608 true] [17592186357344 1111 #uuid "7a8705fc-991a-530c-a9e0-d45dc8ea6831" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357345 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357346 13194139535608 true] [17592186357345 1089 "q-106685" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357345 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535608 true] [17592186357345 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068362/assets/32375f839dd0f51a8624bebda732d7413130c940045db7e5a1a9fce3576e91b6.png)\n\nOne branch of a hyperbola (shown above) is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357345 1113 #uuid "4002f7a8-11ca-5268-8529-2e1c2c8cfac5" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357345 1145 "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a single branch, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068362/assets/d44195c764b2943c3d5b5e0d91ee770011c951d7a825f0c5cc4d1f38cedbb709.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ we get only the upper branch.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe only the upper branch are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).\n$$" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357346 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357347 13194139535608 true] [17592186357346 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357348 13194139535608 true] [17592186357346 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357349 13194139535608 true] [17592186357346 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357350 13194139535608 true] [17592186357346 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357351 13194139535608 true] [17592186357346 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535608 true] [17592186357346 1041 "selection" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357346 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357347 13194139535608 true] [17592186357346 1110 #uuid "f14aa825-c4f3-5e54-9cd2-d57d683c2d15" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357347 1034 "t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357347 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535608 true] [17592186357347 1111 #uuid "e6e2d190-586a-5283-a92b-ca666e36d4a5" 13194139535