emy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068362/assets/46c9d9139a3cff2a76871c69deeac60492d2c9aef4bf1f7ac07a16868d31d6e0.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ we get only the upper branch.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe only the upper branch are\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).\n$$" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357353 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357354 13194139535608 true] [17592186357353 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357355 13194139535608 true] [17592186357353 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357356 13194139535608 true] [17592186357353 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357357 13194139535608 true] [17592186357353 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357358 13194139535608 true] [17592186357353 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535608 true] [17592186357353 1041 "selection" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357353 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357354 13194139535608 true] [17592186357353 1110 #uuid "f3bdd91e-1ea6-5d0a-be55-5e94695fd3c7" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357354 1034 "t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357354 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535608 true] [17592186357354 1111 #uuid "57897eda-42bc-5dba-b320-d8a3d9ba2188" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357355 1034 "t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357355 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535608 true] [17592186357355 1111 #uuid "5e7a1b71-fc81-5788-8fb2-bac3e38283bd" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357356 1034 "t\\in [0,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357356 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535608 true] [17592186357356 1111 #uuid "cdf8bf47-2c56-53ce-8177-0d9d7e78d12b" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357357 1034 "t\\in [-\\pi ,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\cup (\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357357 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535608 true] [17592186357357 1111 #uuid "38248df6-45d9-5619-a06e-bc2bfaeec2e3" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357358 1034 "t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne 0" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357358 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535608 true] [17592186357358 1111 #uuid "4e1cf1d2-8c03-578f-be36-af20697303b6" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357359 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357360 13194139535608 true] [17592186357359 1089 "q-89768" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357359 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535608 true] [17592186357359 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068362/assets/432f8963425031983284db54310c8ae604bc993de66494dceb48e6a4e2bcdf73.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the hyperbola shown above given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{7}{6}x.$" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357359 1113 #uuid "a8a0ddc8-972a-5f01-829a-2b6930d2f171" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357359 1145 "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(0,\\pm a).$ From the graph, we have that $(0,-7)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=7.$\n\nRecall also that the asymptotes of the hyperbola occur at $y=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{7}{6}x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{b} & =\\frac{7}{6} \\\\ \\frac{7}{b} & =\\frac{7}{6} \\\\ b & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=7\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" 13194139535608 true] [17592186357360 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357361 13194139535608 true] [17592186357360 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357362 13194139535608 true] [17592186357360 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357363 13194139535608 true] [17592186357360 1000 #e